.el .ds Aq '
.TH ngx-undo 1  "ngx-undo " 
.SH NAME
ngx\-undo \- Undo a change: restore every file it touched (default: the latest change)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBngx\-undo\fR [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIID\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Undo a change: restore every file it touched (default: the latest change)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Don\*(Aqt ask for confirmation
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be restored without changing anything
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fIID\fR]
Change ID from `ngx history`
.SH EXTRA
The undo itself is validated with nginx \-t like any change, and recorded, so it can be undone too.

Examples:
  sudo ngx undo
  sudo ngx undo 20261101\-101500
